---Panels automatically position components along the panel's direction, resizing them so as to maximize the amount of
---space occupied by the components without exceeding the panel's dimensions. This makes them the ideal method for
---quickly authoring interfaces with consistent layouts, regardless of screen size.
---
---Component positioning is fairly straightforward - left to right for horizontal ones, or top to bottom for vertical
---panels. Resizing meanwhile is more complex as it calculates the amount of empty space based on the panel's dimensions
---and the sum of all component's requested dimensions, and uses that to drive any percentage based calculations.
---
---Warning: As per the above, this means that if multiple components are using offset-based size values and those exceed
---the panel's dimensions, some components will be trimmed or missing.
---@class ui.Panel : ui.ComponentCollection
---@field isVertical boolean If true, child components will be positioned in order from the top to the bottom, otherwise a horizontal layout will be used. Changing this will trigger a layout operation on all child components.
---@field spacing integer The size of the gap between components in interface units. Changing this will trigger a layout operation on all child components.
ui.Panel = {}

---Creates a new Panel on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this panel in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.Panel # The newly created panel. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.Panel.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end
